Preparing a workrave source snapshot for Debian
===============================================

1- Download latest tarball from Github (https://github.com/rcaelers/workrave/downloads).
2- Find latest version number mentioned in the commit log and make a note of the
   last commit ID (https://github.com/rcaelers/workrave/commits/master).
3- Unpack the tarball to a new workrave-LAST_VERSION+COMMIT_ID/ directory
4- Run ./autogen.sh in the tarball
5- Delete these generated files: rm -rf autom4te.cache/ po/Makefile.in.in~
6- Create a new workrave-LAST_VERSION+COMMIT_ID.tar.gz based on that directory

Once a tarball is available, then it's just a matter of using the usual git-buildpackage
tool:

  git import-orig ../workrave-LAST_VERSION+COMMIT_ID.tar.gz

 -- Francois Marier <francois@debian.org>  Mon, 28 May 2012 10:58:05 +1200
